name genome-absolute-refused
timeout 60

# THE GENOME BOUNDARY BITES — doc/doctrine-evolution.md §2.2, and it is a question of SYNTAX rather
# than of discipline.
#
# `pilot_energy_frac` is a `Scale` key: the speed the pursuer insists on keeping, as a MULTIPLE of its
# own `BfmCornerSpeedKt`. The airframe's own number is 380 kt ([MESS] `make -C sim test-corner`). This
# file writes exactly that number into the gene — the most plausible mistake an optimiser or an author
# can make, because 380 is the right answer to the wrong question.
#
# It does not fly. A `Scale` band is dimensionless (0.7…1.2), so a value carrying a dimension is out of
# band whatever the dimension is, and `FBPilotTuning::Set` refuses it before the run starts. The other
# half of the rule is a `static_assert` in `pilot/FBPilotTuning.cpp`: a `Scale` entry whose band is not
# dimensionless, or which names no airframe hook, does not COMPILE. Between the two there is no
# spelling of an absolute in a gene.
#
# READING RULE: exit 1 is the PASS. events.log must carry
#   ERROR module SET_INVALID_VALUE key=pilot_energy_frac value=380
#   ERROR mission SET_REJECTED key=pilot_energy_frac value=380
# and the run must never start. Its twin `genome-scale-flown.fbm` is the same file with the same gene
# at 0.85 — in band, flown, and it moves the throttle.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.40000 4000 90.0 400
  set gear up
  set task bfm
  set pilot_energy_frac 380
  wp 46.90000 7.00000 4000 400
